    "description": "A handsome pair of substantial sterling silver rings featuring mixed-metal detailing, artisan styling, and distinctive design.\nThe first ring features a warm gold-tone band accented by a bezel-set faceted red stone. Interior hallmarks include “STERLING,” “.925,” and “14K,” confirming precious-metal markings for both sterling silver and 14K gold. The photographed scale shows this ring at approximately 2.375 grams. The identity of the red stone has not been verified.\nThe second ring is a wide sterling silver band featuring dimensional geometric and leaf-like detailing with decorative beaded borders and a Southwestern-inspired appearance. The interior is visibly stamped “925,” indicating sterling silver. The photographed scale shows this ring at approximately 3.300 grams.\nTogether, the pair offers an attractive combination of sterling silver, mixed-metal character, gemstone styling, and handcrafted appeal. Both show signs consistent with previous wear, including surface variation and patina. Please review all photographs for hallmark, design, and condition details.\nTotal Photographed Weight: Approximately 5.675 grams combined.\nCollector / Reseller Note:\nThe visible 925/STERLING and 14K hallmarks add particular interest for precious-metal jewelry buyers and resellers. The mixed-metal red-stone ring and decorative sterling band may also appeal to collectors of artisan, Southwestern-inspired, and vintage-style jewelry. Stone identity, maker, age, and origin are not confirmed.",
